WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.585 --> 00:00:04.129
- Are you the best player
in the draft class?

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:05.380
- I feel like I am, yeah.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.259
- [Announcer:] Second steal for
the Ant-Man and the flush.

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:12.429
Edwards launches and connects.

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:14.097
- Reverse it if you can, please.

00:00:14.097 --> 00:00:15.348
- Oh, OK.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:18.184
- Are they teaming up?
- They're teaming up.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.478
- [Announcer:] Impacts the game
in a lot of ways.

00:00:20.478 --> 00:00:21.855
- [Taylor Rooks:]
When we were talking about KD,

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.357
you said you think
he's the greatest player.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.026
- [Anthony Edwards:] Yeah.
- [Taylor:] Ever or right now?

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.068
- Ever.
- Really?

00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:32.866
♪♪♪

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.200
- What's up, guys?
Anthony Edwards here,

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.703
shooting guard
for University of Georgia,

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:37.954
diehard Atlanta guy.

00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:39.873
I'm about to enter
the NBA draft,

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.125
and I'm about to take it there
with Taylor Rooks.

00:00:44.335 --> 00:00:46.087
- Thank you for having me
at UGA.

00:00:46.087 --> 00:00:48.673
I feel like I'm back in college.

00:00:48.673 --> 00:00:50.341
So take me to a college campus.

00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:51.760
Walk me through
your daily routine.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.762
- Wake up in the morning,
probably call my guy,

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:55.722
David, to get some breakfast.

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:58.141
Of course, brush my teeth,
wash my face, go to the gym,

00:00:58.141 --> 00:01:00.226
shoot, then have practice,
then come back and play

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.770
Fortnite the whole night
and go to sleep.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.938
- Are you good at Fortnite?

00:01:03.938 --> 00:01:05.065
-Yeah, I'm really good.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.983
- When you do decide
to leave your dorm,

00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:08.818
how crazy is it
walking around campus?

00:01:08.818 --> 00:01:10.737
Like, are you always recognized?

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:13.615
- Yeah, majority of the time
everybody knows me,

00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:14.991
but I try to walk around
with my hood on

00:01:14.991 --> 00:01:16.201
so I don't get
stopped that much.

00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:17.494
- Well, you know,
it was such a big deal

00:01:17.494 --> 00:01:19.120
when you decided to come to UGA

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.498
because you are
such a big recruit.

00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:23.750
And traditionally,
big recruits go to maybe

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.585
some of the blue-blood schools.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:28.046
Was there a moment where you
really did think

00:01:28.046 --> 00:01:29.506
about taking that route?

00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:30.924
- Most definitely.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.425
When I went on my official visit
to Kentucky,

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:33.760
it was exciting.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.054
I mean, who don't wanna
play in Rupp Arena?

00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:39.349
So I was like, "Man, I think
this is where I should go,"

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:43.603
but then I went on an unofficial
to a Texas game, and I was like,

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.855
"You know what? Forget Kentucky,
I'm gonna come here."

00:01:45.855 --> 00:01:47.440
My sister had just had
my nephew,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.484
so I wanted to see him
grow up a little bit

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:50.860
the little time
I did spend in college.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:55.198
So I think that was
the most important thing.

00:01:55.198 --> 00:01:56.324
- All righty.

00:01:56.324 --> 00:01:57.450
You ready for me to beat you
in some Uno?

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.952
- You playing against
three other people, too.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.204
- Yeah, but I really care
about beating you

00:02:01.204 --> 00:02:02.622
cuz you was talking
trash up there.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.457
OK, so who we got here?

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:08.294
We have my sister
and UGA student, Ryan.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:11.381
Justin, who is your trainer,
mentor.

00:02:11.381 --> 00:02:12.966
Tell me what Justin is to you.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.008
- Like a big brother, basically.

00:02:14.008 --> 00:02:16.553
- Yeah, and also about
to be a loser.

00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:17.804
- No, I'm definitely a winner.

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:18.972
- Yeah, about to be a loser
in this game.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.057
- If I lose, he gotta win.
I'll put it like that.

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:23.143
- Oh, I see, one or the other.
OK, you heard that.

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:24.060
- Us against the Rooks.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:25.436
- All right.
Everyone gets seven.

00:02:25.436 --> 00:02:28.982
Justin, Anthony ready
for the NBA?

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:29.983
- Always ready.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.359
- What's it like training him?

00:02:31.359 --> 00:02:33.570
- From when I started until now,
it got a lot easier.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.655
When he first started, you know,
he was one of those young guys

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:38.158
that not used to the hard work
until it rubbed off on him,

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:40.201
but I can tell you,
once it rubbed off on him,

00:02:40.201 --> 00:02:42.162
he'll call me to get
in the gym now.

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:43.538
- [Taylor:] Yeah?
- Wait, wait,

00:02:43.538 --> 00:02:46.916
so if the, if the line

00:02:46.916 --> 00:02:49.210
is under the number,
is that a nine?

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.336
- [Justin:] Yeah.
- OK, cool.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.754
- No, a s–
It's a nine if it's

00:02:51.754 --> 00:02:54.716
- [Justin:] That's a nine.
- OK, yeah.

00:02:54.716 --> 00:02:56.551
- Even though I showed
you my hand, we good.

00:02:56.551 --> 00:02:59.470
- Yeah, I know everything
you got going, cuh.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.806
- OK, so you talk a lot
about hard work.

00:03:01.806 --> 00:03:03.474
Where do you think
that motivation

00:03:03.474 --> 00:03:05.602
to be a hard worker
comes from?

00:03:05.602 --> 00:03:06.477
- My big brother.

00:03:06.477 --> 00:03:08.980
When I was in the ninth grade,
I didn't work that hard.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.690
Everything I did on the court
was just based off

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.400
God-given talents
and abilities that

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.777
He gave me, and my brother used
to wake up early in the morning

00:03:14.777 --> 00:03:16.988
and go shoot and go work out,
like, on game days.

00:03:16.988 --> 00:03:18.865
So I wanted to be like him.
So I was like,

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:20.366
"Man, I'm fittin' to start
getting up and working out."

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.826
- [ Taylor:] Yeah.
- [Anthony:] It was hard because

00:03:21.826 --> 00:03:23.328
a lotta stuff
that I did with my trainer,

00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:25.455
I couldn't really do cuz
I was never really working out.

00:03:25.455 --> 00:03:27.582
I was getting frustrated cuz
I couldn't do this move

00:03:27.582 --> 00:03:29.667
or make this shot
or, you know, do something.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:31.878
So I was like, "Man, I'm fittin'
to get in here every day

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:34.047
so it can be
second nature to me."

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:38.051
- When did you realize,
"OK, I'm different.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:41.554
Like, I'm separated from the
pack a little bit. I'm elite."

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:44.390
- [Anthony:] Probably the
Under Armour All-America camp.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.893
I think I was in, like,
10th grade.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:49.896
Everybody else was older
than me, and I was just killing.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.731
Like, every game I was killing,
and I was like,

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.733
"Man, I think I'm better
than everybody in here."

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.901
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:57.403
- Who–Was there any notable
names there that we would know?

00:03:57.403 --> 00:04:03.076
- Yeah, Jahvon Quinerly,
Trevon Duval, Naz Reid.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:04.327
- OK, very nice.

00:04:04.327 --> 00:04:06.412
I watched an interview,
and you said

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:10.083
that an NBA player
told you that,

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.168
"You can tell a guy is ready
to go to the next level

00:04:12.168 --> 00:04:13.836
when they seem like
they're bored, like,

00:04:13.836 --> 00:04:15.338
with what they're playing."
- Yeah.

00:04:15.338 --> 00:04:17.590
- Do you feel bored now at all?

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.800
- Yes and no.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.635
Yes because I get doubled,
like, every game.

00:04:20.635 --> 00:04:21.886
I get denied every game.

00:04:21.886 --> 00:04:24.472
So it gets boring, and it gets
frustrating

00:04:24.472 --> 00:04:26.266
because I can't do
what I wanna do

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.600
and give the fans
what they wanna see

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.310
because I'm getting doubled
all the time,

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:30.603
and they're locked in on me,

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:33.231
but no because,
I mean, my teammates,

00:04:33.231 --> 00:04:35.566
and they always
make it fun for me, so.

00:04:35.566 --> 00:04:37.318
I love my teammates.
They're like my brothers, so.

00:04:37.318 --> 00:04:39.862
- The person who goes No. 1,

00:04:39.862 --> 00:04:42.490
what are the expectations
of the No. 1 pick?

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.410
- I feel like to just come in
and impact the game immediately.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.996
Like, whatever team you go to,
just show them that you can win.

00:04:47.996 --> 00:04:49.455
- And you can win?
- Yeah.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.082
- [Taylor:] Yeah?
What makes you a winner?

00:04:51.082 --> 00:04:52.292
- [Anthony:]
My competitive nature.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.126
I always wanna compete.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:56.170
I wanna go against the best
every time I step on the floor.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:02.010
- All right, Ryan, so, like,
as a student here, like,

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.137
what are people
saying about Anthony?

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:06.472
- Well, like, Georgia's
a huge football school,

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.141
but now that you're here,
people are like,

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:09.851
"Oh, my gosh,
are we finally becoming

00:05:09.851 --> 00:05:13.104
a basketball school?"
Like, "Oh, my gosh!"

00:05:13.104 --> 00:05:14.647
- What do you think
it would take for UGA

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:15.857
to be a basketball school?

00:05:15.857 --> 00:05:17.775
- We gotta win, so.
And we gotta get players.

00:05:17.775 --> 00:05:19.485
So that's why I came here
so they'll see

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:20.987
that I came
so they'll start coming,

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:22.530
and more players
will try to stay at home.

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:23.656
- Yeah?
Do you feel like

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.366
more people
are going to basketball games?

00:05:25.366 --> 00:05:26.659
- Definitely.
- Yeah?

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.536
- [Ryan:] Yes.

00:05:28.536 --> 00:05:31.080
- OK, before I put
this card down, I know

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.041
Uno may be
one of your weaknesses,

00:05:33.041 --> 00:05:35.043
but what's your weakness
as a player?

00:05:35.043 --> 00:05:36.085
- Hmm, whatchu think?

00:05:36.085 --> 00:05:37.337
- I think his weakness might be

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:39.797
just staying engaged
for 40 minutes.

00:05:39.797 --> 00:05:41.174
It's not about what he can't do.

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:43.259
It's about, "Is he gonna
do it all the time?"

00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:45.428
- Would you agree? Yeah?
- Yeah.

00:05:45.428 --> 00:05:47.180
- What do you feel
about your shot selection?

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:50.308
- Sometimes bad, but being
how I'm guarded,

00:05:50.308 --> 00:05:51.851
sometimes I gotta
take bad shots.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.644
- [Taylor:] Yeah, you gotta do
what you gotta do?

00:05:53.644 --> 00:05:55.021
- Yeah.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:58.483
- Well, right now, you gotta
put down a blue if you have it.

00:05:58.483 --> 00:06:01.194
- Mmm, that's so clutch.

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:02.862
- [Justin:] Ooh.
- [Anthony:] That's so clutch.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.742
- So let's talk the draft.

00:06:07.742 --> 00:06:09.452
Are you the best player
in the draft class?

00:06:09.452 --> 00:06:10.661
- I feel like I am, yeah.

00:06:10.661 --> 00:06:12.205
- Yeah?
What do you think separates you?

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:13.790
- I feel like me
on the defensive end. Like,

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.792
if I lock in every time
on the defensive end,

00:06:15.792 --> 00:06:17.210
nobody is better than me
in the draft.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.420
Of course, I feel like I can
score the ball the best,

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:21.506
pass, rebound,
all types of stuff,

00:06:21.506 --> 00:06:23.549
but I feel like defense
is gonna separate

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:25.009
everybody in the draft, yeah.

00:06:25.009 --> 00:06:27.345
- [Taylor:] So you feel like you
deserve to be the No. 1 pick?

00:06:27.345 --> 00:06:28.554
- Yeah.
- [Taylor:] OK.

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:30.348
A lot of really good guys
in your draft class,

00:06:30.348 --> 00:06:33.184
so let's talk about
some of them.

00:06:33.184 --> 00:06:36.479
Give me an evaluation
of Cole Anthony.

00:06:36.479 --> 00:06:38.064
- I never really played
against him, so.

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:39.399
- Mmhmm.
- Like, I played with him.

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:42.568
He's really good at picking
roles. Like, he real smart.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:43.986
He can pass.
He can shoot.

00:06:43.986 --> 00:06:45.530
He's a great player
if you ask me, yeah.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:48.574
- Yeah. Give me an evaluation
of James Wiseman.

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:50.785
- I love James.
He's 7 feet.

00:06:50.785 --> 00:06:53.246
Can shoot, run the floor
like no other,

00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:55.790
plays hard, don't really
complain about the ball.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:57.166
If he want the ball,
he's gonna let you know

00:06:57.166 --> 00:06:58.251
he want the ball.

00:06:58.251 --> 00:06:59.919
A great person on
and off the court.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:01.170
- LaMelo Ball?

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:02.880
- [Anthony:]
Really good point guard at,

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.006
like, 6'7", 6'8", I guess.

00:07:04.006 --> 00:07:06.801
I don't know.
Flashy point guard.

00:07:06.801 --> 00:07:08.052
- [Taylor:] OK.

00:07:08.052 --> 00:07:09.595
We are going to walk through
some of the teams

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:11.764
that could maybe draft you,
OK?

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.808
You give me your thoughts
on those teams.

00:07:13.808 --> 00:07:16.185
-OK.
- All right. New York Knicks.

00:07:16.185 --> 00:07:18.438
- I mean, New York
I'd play for anywhere.

00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:20.022
I definitely can fit
with the Knicks.

00:07:20.022 --> 00:07:22.108
They, like, they in need
of, like, a shooting guard,

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:23.651
a point guard, whatever.

00:07:23.651 --> 00:07:25.069
Whatever position they wanna
put me at,

00:07:25.069 --> 00:07:26.070
I'm ready to play it.
- Yeah?

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:26.904
- [Anthony:] Yeah.

00:07:26.904 --> 00:07:27.864
- [Taylor:]
OK, Cleveland Cavaliers.

00:07:27.864 --> 00:07:30.825
- Cleveland got a dude I'm
real cool with, Collin Sexton.

00:07:30.825 --> 00:07:32.160
He's from Atlanta.
- [Taylor:] Yeah?

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.620
- [Anthony:] Yeah, I would love
to play with Cleveland.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:35.997
- Golden State Warriors.

00:07:35.997 --> 00:07:38.082
- Oh, who wouldn't love to play
with Stephen Curry,

00:07:38.082 --> 00:07:39.459
Klay Thompson
and Draymond Green?

00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:40.543
They're gonna be great

00:07:40.543 --> 00:07:42.044
and could make me better
at all times,

00:07:42.044 --> 00:07:43.296
so, yeah, I'd love
to play with them.

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:44.797
- Atlanta Hawks?

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:47.467
- That's my home, so that'd
be like a dream come true

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:48.926
if I play for the Hawks.

00:07:48.926 --> 00:07:50.344
I'm real cool
with Trae Young, so.

00:07:50.344 --> 00:07:52.180
- [Taylor:] Yeah?
- [Anthony:] And Cam Reddish,

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:53.931
so, like, playing for the Hawks
would be crazy.

00:07:53.931 --> 00:07:55.224
- [Taylor:] All right.

00:07:55.224 --> 00:07:58.394
Speaking of winners,
I have two surprises for you,

00:07:58.394 --> 00:07:59.645
OK?

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:03.232
I had two friends of mine
send in a video for you.

00:08:03.232 --> 00:08:04.567
- [Michael Vick:]
Taylor, what up?

00:08:04.567 --> 00:08:06.486
I know you're sitting down
with Anthony today.

00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:09.447
Tell Anthony I said,
"What's up?"

00:08:09.447 --> 00:08:12.783
Tell him I said, "The hard work
gonna pay off in the future.

00:08:12.783 --> 00:08:14.869
He's in this position
for a reason."

00:08:14.869 --> 00:08:16.454
I hope y'all have
a good interview,

00:08:16.454 --> 00:08:18.498
and I hope some good things
come from it.

00:08:18.498 --> 00:08:19.665
- You're a big Michael Vick fan,
right?

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:21.292
- Yeah, most definitely.

00:08:21.292 --> 00:08:22.668
- What's it like seeing that?

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:23.503
- [Anthony:] To me,

00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:25.254
he's the greatest
quarterback to ever play.

00:08:25.254 --> 00:08:27.632
I love Michael Vick, so seeing
that just, like I said,

00:08:27.632 --> 00:08:28.841
drives me
to keep working hard.

00:08:28.841 --> 00:08:31.344
- Yeah, and it's crazy,
you know.

00:08:31.344 --> 00:08:33.513
He, like, watches this stuff.
When I told him

00:08:33.513 --> 00:08:34.889
that I was gonna do
this interview, he's like,

00:08:34.889 --> 00:08:36.516
"Oh, I know who Anthony is.
I'd love to send one."

00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:37.892
Want me to show you
the second video?

00:08:37.892 --> 00:08:39.685
- Yo, what's up, Ant?
- My guy.

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:41.020
- Victor Oladipo here, man.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.230
First and foremost,
just wanna let you know

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:43.564
I'm a big fan of yours.

00:08:43.564 --> 00:08:45.525
Just continue to keep
getting better, bro.

00:08:45.525 --> 00:08:47.527
Like, you got
the talent already.

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:49.862
