that you have in the NBA?

00:12:57.234 --> 00:13:00.446
- Well, actually, I didn't meet
D-Wade from Coach Crean.

00:13:00.446 --> 00:13:02.490
I met D-Wade from his son,
who was at Pangos

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:04.450
All-American Camp,
and me and his son

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:05.743
happened to be teammates.

00:13:05.743 --> 00:13:07.745
And at the time, his son
didn't know who I was,

00:13:07.745 --> 00:13:10.122
but at the camp,
I went, like, crazy.

00:13:10.122 --> 00:13:11.874
So, like, going between
the legs,

00:13:11.874 --> 00:13:13.918
dunking on people,
like, shooting,

00:13:13.918 --> 00:13:16.170
scoring all type of ways.

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:17.963
And I guess his son's friend,

00:13:17.963 --> 00:13:19.965
who was, like,
his assistant down there,

00:13:19.965 --> 00:13:21.342
called him and was like,

00:13:21.342 --> 00:13:23.260
"Yo, there's this kid
on Zaire's team.

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:25.679
He's really good.
Like, he's really, really good."

00:13:25.679 --> 00:13:27.139
Then, like, next thing you know,
he followed me,

00:13:27.139 --> 00:13:29.266
and we was texting
and stuff like that, yeah.

00:13:29.266 --> 00:13:30.309
- Oh, that's great.
- [Anthony:] Yeah.

00:13:30.309 --> 00:13:31.477
- OK, what about Victor?

00:13:31.477 --> 00:13:32.686
- [Anthony:]
Vic started texting me

00:13:32.686 --> 00:13:33.479
when he found out, like,

00:13:33.479 --> 00:13:35.147
I was goin' to play
for Coach Crean.

00:13:35.147 --> 00:13:36.232
- [Taylor:] Yeah?

00:13:36.232 --> 00:13:37.608
- Then we just gained a really
good relationship.

00:13:37.608 --> 00:13:38.818
- And what about Trae Young?

00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:40.945
- [Anthony:] Trae a young guy,
so we been knew each other,

00:13:40.945 --> 00:13:43.656
and now it's just like he want
me to come play with him, so–

00:13:43.656 --> 00:13:44.949
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

00:13:44.949 --> 00:13:46.242
- Yeah, what's that like?

00:13:46.242 --> 00:13:48.410
So is Trae like,
"Man, Atlanta's gotta get you.

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:50.329
Atlanta's gotta draft you"?
- Yeah, just like Ja Morant.

00:13:50.329 --> 00:13:51.747
- Yeah.
- Me and Ja Morant real cool.

00:13:51.747 --> 00:13:53.040
He want me to
come play with him.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.291
- [Taylor:] Really?
- [Anthony:] Yeah.

00:13:54.291 --> 00:13:55.793
- What's that friendship like,
you and Ja?

00:13:55.793 --> 00:13:57.503
- I would love to play with Ja.
- Yeah.

00:13:57.503 --> 00:13:59.296
- I mean, he's super,
super good,

00:13:59.296 --> 00:14:01.715
and he love to pass the ball.
- [Taylor:] Mmhmm.

00:14:01.715 --> 00:14:03.175
- So I'd love to play
with somebody like that.

00:14:03.175 --> 00:14:05.302
- Yeah, and he's a dunker,
which is always fun.

00:14:05.302 --> 00:14:06.887
- Yeah.
- [Taylor:] Yeah.

00:14:09.557 --> 00:14:11.642
So basketball, you know,
is always evolving.

00:14:11.642 --> 00:14:14.603
You had, like, fast-break game,
post game, iso game.

00:14:14.603 --> 00:14:17.022
Now we're very positionless.

00:14:17.022 --> 00:14:19.316
What type of game do you prefer?

00:14:19.316 --> 00:14:21.193
- I like playing fast
cuz I feel like

00:14:21.193 --> 00:14:23.529
I play my best ball
scoring early in the shot clock,

00:14:23.529 --> 00:14:25.698
like, eight seconds,
first eight seconds.

00:14:25.698 --> 00:14:27.157
- Do you think you're
a positionless player?

00:14:27.157 --> 00:14:29.159
- Yeah, I can be.
I can play the 1 or the 2,

00:14:29.159 --> 00:14:30.870
nothing more than that,
but, yeah.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:32.788
- [Taylor:]
Nothing more than that, OK.

00:14:32.788 --> 00:14:33.956
- [Justin:] Green.

00:14:33.956 --> 00:14:36.166
- No, no, no, no.
- [Justin:] Oh, my bad.

00:14:36.166 --> 00:14:37.668
- But I gotta do this to you.

00:14:37.668 --> 00:14:38.878
- [Justin:]
You go ahead and do it.

00:14:38.878 --> 00:14:41.463
Do it. Go ahead and do it.
Just get it over with.

00:14:41.463 --> 00:14:42.423
- That yellow card.

00:14:42.423 --> 00:14:44.633
- We would never do that.
No.

00:14:44.633 --> 00:14:46.677
- Don't let them,
don't let them do that, now.

00:14:46.677 --> 00:14:47.970
- We gotta get in between them.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:49.138
- Yo, we good. We good.
We good.

00:14:49.138 --> 00:14:50.264
- Don't let them do that.

00:14:52.725 --> 00:14:55.060
- What's your favorite movie?

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:56.061
- "Matilda."

00:14:56.061 --> 00:14:57.646
- "Matilda."
You have to explain

00:14:57.646 --> 00:14:58.981
why your favorite movie
is "Matilda."

00:14:58.981 --> 00:15:02.318
- Because I feel like women
are powerful, so Matilda,

00:15:02.318 --> 00:15:05.863
I mean, she was a very powerful
little girl at such a young age,

00:15:05.863 --> 00:15:07.573
and I just like
to see things like that.

00:15:07.573 --> 00:15:09.450
So when I first seen it,
I was like,

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:11.493
"This is the best movie
of all time."

00:15:11.493 --> 00:15:13.913
- The best movie of all time,
I love that answer.

00:15:13.913 --> 00:15:16.248
I know that you've had some
very strong women

00:15:16.248 --> 00:15:17.958
in your life:
your mom, your grandma.

00:15:17.958 --> 00:15:19.585
I wanna give you a chance
to just talk

00:15:19.585 --> 00:15:22.171
about the impact
that they had on you.

00:15:22.171 --> 00:15:24.298
- Like, working hard,
I got it from both of them.

00:15:24.298 --> 00:15:25.966
They always worked late night.

00:15:25.966 --> 00:15:28.260
They was the best people
I ever had in my life that

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:29.678
I ever met, yeah.
- Yeah?

00:15:29.678 --> 00:15:32.723
What have you learned
from having to deal with loss

00:15:32.723 --> 00:15:34.141
at such a young age?
- Don't let things rattle me.

00:15:34.141 --> 00:15:35.517
I don't really let nothing
bother me

00:15:35.517 --> 00:15:36.769
cuz of what I've been through,
so.

00:15:36.769 --> 00:15:38.312
Feel like people coming to me

00:15:38.312 --> 00:15:40.689
complaining about this,
about that, I'm like,

00:15:40.689 --> 00:15:44.193
"Dude, there's always a way."
- Yeah.

00:15:44.193 --> 00:15:45.694
- So I always try
to tell people that.

00:15:45.694 --> 00:15:46.862
Man, there's always a way.

00:15:46.862 --> 00:15:48.280
God got something
better for you.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:49.698
- You say there's always a way.

00:15:49.698 --> 00:15:52.868
When you were maybe feeling,
like, down, probably basketball,

00:15:52.868 --> 00:15:54.870
I don't know, was this season
difficult for you

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:56.956
with not having
a winning record

00:15:56.956 --> 00:15:59.291
and experiencing losses
on the court?

00:15:59.291 --> 00:16:01.585
- Losing is always bad,
but you just gotta look at it

00:16:01.585 --> 00:16:03.837
like I'm blessed to wake up
the next day and play the game.

00:16:03.837 --> 00:16:05.798
So we were always worried
about the next game.

00:16:05.798 --> 00:16:06.966
No matter what happened
this game,

00:16:06.966 --> 00:16:08.300
we worry about
the next game after that.

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:11.637
- Why did you select No. 5
as your jersey number?

00:16:11.637 --> 00:16:15.557
- My mom passed on January 5,
and my grandma on July 5, so.

00:16:15.557 --> 00:16:17.101
My birthday is on the fifth.

00:16:17.101 --> 00:16:18.644
My sister's birthday
on the fifth.

00:16:18.644 --> 00:16:21.480
So, I mean, it's a lotta fives
going on around, so.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:22.898
- [Taylor:] Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:16:22.898 --> 00:16:24.817
- OK. When you go to the NBA,
you have to wear No. 5?

00:16:24.817 --> 00:16:26.402
- [Anthony:] I pray to God
they let me get it.

00:16:26.402 --> 00:16:27.820
- [Taylor:] Yeah?
- [Anthony:] Yeah.

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:30.114
- You don't seem like you get
very rattled by anything.

00:16:30.114 --> 00:16:30.990
- No, not really.

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:32.533
- OK, then what rattles you?

00:16:32.533 --> 00:16:34.743
Something has to rattle you.

00:16:34.743 --> 00:16:37.538
- Being in the dark.
- [ Laughing]

00:16:37.538 --> 00:16:39.748
- That's it.
If I can see what's going on,

00:16:39.748 --> 00:16:40.958
I'm not rattled at all.

00:16:40.958 --> 00:16:42.668
- OK, opponents, take note.

00:16:42.668 --> 00:16:45.963
You wanna beat Anthony,
turn off the electricity.

00:16:45.963 --> 00:16:48.007
- Nah, I'mma get up
out of there.

00:16:48.007 --> 00:16:50.175
- You have a nightlight?
- Nah, I ain't got no night–

00:16:50.175 --> 00:16:52.011
nah, I ain't got
no nightlight, no.

00:16:52.011 --> 00:16:55.180
♪♪♪

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:56.974
- What's his player
comparison?

00:16:56.974 --> 00:16:58.684
- He doesn't have a true player
comparison.

00:16:58.684 --> 00:17:00.102
He's like a mixture
between guys.

00:17:00.102 --> 00:17:01.979
You gotta take a little bit
from this guy and that guy.

00:17:01.979 --> 00:17:03.689
He's unique the way he moves.

00:17:03.689 --> 00:17:05.691
He moves like a smaller guy,
a guard,

00:17:05.691 --> 00:17:06.775
but he's a bigger guard,

00:17:06.775 --> 00:17:08.318
and then when you find
a bigger guard,

00:17:08.318 --> 00:17:09.695
they don't move like him,
and they're not as athletic.

00:17:09.695 --> 00:17:11.030
- Yeah.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:12.364
- Or they're athletic
and they can't shoot.

00:17:12.364 --> 00:17:13.949
So he's like a mixture between
a few different people.

00:17:13.949 --> 00:17:15.075
- [Taylor:] OK.
- [Justin:] Yeah.

